# Simple OS 1.1.2
## Better menus
- **The row under the mouse lights up.** In the start menu, the search and the menus of the taskbar, the row you point
  at is highlighted in your accent color – the same as with the arrow keys.
- **The best match comes first.** Type "Sound" in the start menu and Sound is at the top.
- **Settings in the search.** Search for "display settings" (or sound, Wi-Fi, keyboard …) and the right page of the
  Control Center opens.
- **The sound menu stays open** while you change the volume, and menus opened from the start menu appear faster.
## Fixed
- **Desktop PCs lock again after a video.** After watching a video, a computer without a battery no longer locked the
  screen when it turned off.
- **Do Not Disturb stays on** after signing out and after a restart, until you turn it off.
- **Clearer update window.** It counts the updates ("Update 3 of 14") without technical lines from apps, and no longer
  flickers at the end.
- **Nothing left behind after signing out.** Two small taskbar helpers kept running after signing out.
## Fixed in 1.1.1
- **Menus stay open after a slow click.** The desktop and window menus no longer close when you hold the mouse
  button a little longer.
- **The speaker icon opens the sound menu.** A click on the speaker in the taskbar used to mute the sound; now it
  opens volume and outputs. Scroll over it for louder/quieter, middle-click to mute.
- **Notification menus on big screens.** The menu with a notification's buttons now grows with the display scale.
- **Bigger window buttons.** Minimize, maximize and close are larger and easier to hit; close turns red under the
  pointer.
- **Updates in plain words.** The update window counts the updates instead of showing technical package lines, and
  a restore point no longer looks stuck at 0 %.
- **Each software store has its own icon.** The Software Center and the Software Store are easy to tell apart.
## New in 1.1
- **Scale for screens with many pixels.** Control Center → Display → Scale makes text, the taskbar, menus,
  notifications and the mouse pointer bigger. "Automatic" picks it from your screen's size (2.8K and 4K laptops), or
  choose 125, 150 or 200 % yourself.
- **Language & Region.** Change the language of your apps and the format of dates, numbers and currency in Control
  Center → Language & Region. Spell checking and the Firefox and LibreOffice languages come with it. Simple OS's own
  tools (Control Center, Setup, Software Updates) stay in English for now – their translations come in 1.2.
- **Camera.** Menu → Apps → Camera shows your webcam and takes photos – they are saved in Pictures/Camera.
- **A larger taskbar.** Control Center → Appearance → Taskbar → Layout → Large: a higher bar with a bigger clock.
- **Starting up is quicker.** The files the computer loads at startup are now much smaller.
## Also fixed in 1.1
- **"Safely remove" only for USB drives.** A second internal disk (with Windows or another Linux on it) no longer
  shows up as a USB drive.
